Support for Custom Help Text in Built-in help Function
======================================================

The built-in help function primarily grabs from Python's docs (see the Doc
folder).  The files in this directory are used to generate
pydoc_data.bespoke_help, which is used to provide additional specialized
information about certain topics (as a foreword of sorts).

To add new bespoke help text, you have a few options:

  * Adding a plain-text file containing help text to
    Tools/pydoc/bespoke/topics/MY_TOPIC.txt will cause that text to show up
    verbatim when help("MY_TOPIC") is invoked.

  * Adding a function _help_MY_TOPIC() to Tools/pydoc/bespoke/base.py
    will cause that function to be called when help("MY_TOPIC") is invoked.
    Your function should return a string, and that string will be shown
    verbatim.

  * Adding a nullary function as the value associated with the key "MY_TOPIC"
    in _symbol_lookup in Tools/pydocs/bespoke/base.py will cause that function
    to be called when help("MY_TOPIC") is invoked.  As above, your function
    should return a string, which will be shown verbatim.  This option is
    provided as a way to add bespoke help text for topics that aren't valid
    Python variable names (or filenames) such as "<".
